Track 3: Did You Graft the Lightning Seed?
- Story & Context: Locals whisper tales of the storm-station's phantom broadcasts evolving into a protective ward, its djent-riddled signal manifesting as phosphorescent moss that glows brighter with each thunderclap, an ethereal guardian against the deep-sea entities drawn to the desolate Geomun Bay; they say anyone who touches the moss during a deluge finds their own thoughts echoing the lost melodies, caught in the eternal cycle of transmission and decay. "The static remembers every wave."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A towering, ancient lightning-scarred tree, its bark fused with gleaming, geometric metallic plates that resemble radio antennas. Bioluminescent moss, pulsing with soft, erratic light, clings to the metallic trunk, appearing like strange, organic circuitry. Below, a lone, hooded figure with an outstretched hand, tentatively reaching towards the glowing moss as a blinding bolt of lightning dramatically forks in the dark sky above, casting sharp, ephemeral shadows.

